The attached image, Figure 6 from the npj Vaccines PDF, illustrates Nano-11's ability to enhance antigen targeting and retention. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA+ cells in the draining lymph node exhibit the highest expression of the costimulatory molecule CD86, indicating their immunopotentiating capacity. Panel B further phenotypes OVA+ and OVA- MigDCs, showing that OVA is predominantly present in CD11b+ DCs following Nano-11 adjuvanted OVA injection. Panel C presents in vivo fluorescence imaging, demonstrating that while soluble OVA is rapidly cleared from the injection site, OVA adjuvanted with Nano-11 or aluminum hydroxide is retained for a longer duration, with Nano-11 maintaining antigen presence comparably to AH over 7 days.